cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its evaluation protocol, please cite it as below."
title: "Graph Neural Network and Transformer Fusion for Molecular Property Prediction under a Strict Evaluation Protocol: Notation Leakage, Descriptor Baselines and Conformal Coverage"
abstract: >-
  An evaluation protocol for multi-view molecular property prediction, and a fusion
  architecture measured under it. Eight MoleculeNet datasets, six scaffold splits, paired
  comparisons with Holm correction and an across-dataset test, an equivalence test,
  split-conformal uncertainty, and machine-checked reproducibility gates. Finds that SMILES
  notation leaks the label in ClinTox and BBBP; with the leak removed, no fusion variant
  outperforms a fingerprint-plus-descriptor MLP and the advantage over a two-layer graph
  network is not significant across datasets; and minority-class conformal coverage on Tox21
  depends on class weighting in training rather than on the architecture.
type: software

